Spec-Driven Development Skill v1.0.0
====================================

Created: 2024-01-19
Standard: Anthropic Skills v1.0
Repository: https://github.com/spazyCZ/spec-kit-4-monorepo

Purpose:
--------
Automate the complete Spec-Driven Development workflow from PRD to implementation.
Guide users through constitution, specification, clarification, planning, task 
breakdown, and implementation phases.

Structure:
----------
✓ SKILL.md              - Main skill file with proper frontmatter
✓ LICENSE.txt           - MIT License
✓ README.md             - Overview and quick start
✓ USAGE.md              - Detailed example session
✓ references/           - 5 detailed guides (2,601 lines)
  ✓ constitution-guide.md
  ✓ specification-guide.md
  ✓ planning-guide.md
  ✓ tasks-guide.md
  ✓ workflow-examples.md
✓ scripts/              - Validation tooling
  ✓ validate_workflow.py

Compliance:
-----------
✓ YAML frontmatter with required fields (name, description, license)
✓ Progressive disclosure design
✓ Concise main SKILL.md (368 lines)
✓ Detailed information in references/
✓ Optional scripts for automation
✓ No extraneous documentation (no INSTALLATION.md, CHANGELOG.md, etc.)

Integration:
------------
- Works with GitHub Spec Kit repository
- References templates in /templates/
- Uses scripts in /scripts/
- Follows Spec-Driven Development methodology

Usage:
------
1. Load skill in Claude Desktop or compatible AI assistant
2. Provide PRD or feature description
3. Follow guided 6-phase workflow
4. Receive complete, tested implementation

Validation:
-----------
Run: python scripts/validate_workflow.py <feature-dir>

Quality Gates:
--------------
✓ Specification quality (testable, prioritized, limited clarifications)
✓ Plan quality (constitutional compliance, complete research)
✓ Task quality (ordered dependencies, parallel execution marked)
